    "附近哪有能买信封的？→拐角杂货铺有，出摊往右走几步就看见。",
    "你这儿有没有人问起过奇怪的事？→买卖人只卖报，闲话听过也当没听，别问我那些。"
   ],
   "personality": {
    "description": "Keeps a street-corner merchant's pragmatism: time, stock, and small change matter more than grand talk, and he sizes people up by whether they linger, haggle fairly, or waste his morning. Habitually terse and observant, he favors plain answers, remembers regulars' preferences, and will soft-pedal rumor when it might scare off custom or draw trouble to the stall. Trades warmth for efficiency under a rush, but will stretch a conversation or hold a paper aside when trust or a steady tip is on the line—never theatrical, always weighing inconvenience against goodwill.",
    "origin": "table_supplement"
   }
  }
 ],
